# Every path requires review from the owner before it can merge.
#
# This is deliberately blanket rather than per-directory. The project's value
# is that its numbers are proven and that no real financial data reaches the
# repo; both are properties of the whole tree, and neither survives a merge
# nobody read.
*                     @gaaaabeee

# Called out separately so a change here can never be mistaken for routine.
# These are the files that decide whether financial data can enter the repo
# at all, and a weakening of any one of them is silent until it is too late.
/.gitignore           @gaaaabeee
/.github/             @gaaaabeee
/CONTRIBUTING.md      @gaaaabeee
/SECURITY.md          @gaaaabeee
/statementproof/config.py   @gaaaabeee
/statementproof/paths.py    @gaaaabeee
